<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1426037006">
<title>
Intake VVT actuator
</title>
<topic id = "AENLSB0A1426037007">
<title>
Motor part
</title>
<ptxt>
Refer to 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0A1326040">Intake VVT Actuator On-Vehicle Inspection:K14D</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</topic>
<topic id = "AENLSB0A1426037008">
<title>
Sprocket part
</title>
<ptxt>
Remove intake VVT actuator (motor part). Check eccentric shaft (1) of intake VVT actuator (sprocket part) for smooth rotation. If any abnormality is found, replace intake VVT actuator (sprocket part).
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILSB0A132020.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "54.717mm" ver = "01" gw = "165" gh = "139"/>
</figure>
</topic>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1426037004">
<title>
Exhaust VVT Actuator
</title>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Check exhaust VVT actuator for wear or damage.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Replace exhaust VVT actuator if any defect is found.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Hold intake camshaft using spanner or adjustable wrench with exhaust VVT actuator (1) fitted and check that exhaust VVT actuator cannot be turned by hand.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Replace exhaust VVT actuator if it is turned by hand.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILSB0A142098.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "57.268mm" ver = "01" gw = "185" gh = "146"/>
</figure>
</item>
</list1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1426037005">
<title>
Signal Rotor
</title>
<ptxt>
Check signal rotor (1) for crack and damage.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If any defect is found, replace camshaft.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A140220.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "38.699mm" ver = "01" gw = "178" gh = "93"/>
</figure>
</servinfosub>
